WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.090
What exactly is Project Butterfly?

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:05.750
Is Vigilante as crazy as he acts?

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.540
And how did Peacemaker survive the events
of "The Suicide Squad?"

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:13.300
Here's a quick explainer about where the first
three episodes of Peacemaker leave our patriotic

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.300
hero.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.947
"Hey, the reason I'm excited?

00:00:15.947 --> 00:00:17.083
It is normal."

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:20.550
If you didn't catch his appearance in James
Gunn's quasi-reboot "The Suicide Squad" when

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:25.169
it premiered last summer, "Peacemaker" helpfully
brings you up to speed by showcasing exactly

00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:28.809
what the title character's all about:
"I cherish peace with all my heart."

00:00:28.809 --> 00:00:29.809
stabs/shoots guys.

00:00:29.809 --> 00:00:33.269
"I don't care how many men, women, and children
I need to kill to get it."

00:00:33.269 --> 00:00:34.850
What else do you need to know?

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:39.311
After the battle against Starro the Conqueror
in Corto Maltese, Peacemaker is more or less

00:00:39.311 --> 00:00:42.065
right as rain, despite getting shot in the throat, and getting

00:00:42.065 --> 00:00:43.374
a building dropped on him.

00:00:43.781 --> 00:00:48.411
"You're shot and a building falls on you and
all you have to replace is a clavicle?

00:00:48.411 --> 00:00:52.321
You're the luckiest man alive."

00:00:52.321 --> 00:00:56.632
After getting recaptured shortly after leaving
the hospital, Peacemaker's once again back

00:00:56.632 --> 00:01:01.612
working for the government, though Amanda
Waller's not his commanding officer this time.

00:01:01.612 --> 00:01:05.902
Peacemaker's new boss is Clemson Murn, a mercenary
with a dark reputation.

00:01:05.902 --> 00:01:09.802
But it's not all new in "Peacemaker" – the
first hour of the series brings a number of

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:15.741
familiar faces back from Task Force X, including
Emilia Harcourt, John Economos, and, briefly,

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:18.202
a cameo from Amanda Waller herself.

00:01:18.202 --> 00:01:23.572
We also meet a new member of the team, Leota
Adebayo, Peacemaker's racist father, Auggie

00:01:23.572 --> 00:01:28.231
Smith; and Peacemaker's best human friend-slash-biggest-fan
Vigilante.

00:01:28.231 --> 00:01:31.332
Let's take a look at where they all end up
in the first three episodes of "Peacemaker."

00:01:32.622 --> 00:01:37.172
After following Harcourt to a bar, Peacemaker
makes a series of passes at his co-worker,

00:01:37.172 --> 00:01:38.801
none of which work out.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:42.741
Though Peacemaker is immediately attracted
to Harcourt, he becomes even more smitten

00:01:42.741 --> 00:01:45.462
when she violently takes down a man who attacks
her.

00:01:45.462 --> 00:01:49.532
Harcourt later gives Peacemaker a piece of
her mind – not that he totally gets what

00:01:49.532 --> 00:01:50.632
she has to say.

00:01:50.632 --> 00:01:54.112
"I have no interest in you, other than your
ability to fight for us.

00:01:54.112 --> 00:01:56.722
Just because you're handsome, doesn't mean
you're not a piece-of-sh-t murderer."

00:01:56.722 --> 00:01:58.761
"You think I'm handsome?"

00:01:58.761 --> 00:02:02.972
When Peacemaker begs for a no-strings-attached
deal between the two of them, Harcourt appears

00:02:02.972 --> 00:02:05.542
to grow even less interested and leaves.

00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:10.252
While Peacemaker spends a significant amount
of time in the first episode focusing on sex,

00:02:10.252 --> 00:02:14.082
Harcourt appears laser-focused on the finer
details of her new job.

00:02:14.082 --> 00:02:18.552
She sees her placement on this specific task
force as punishment for her participation

00:02:18.552 --> 00:02:22.882
in the mutiny against Amanda Waller in "The
Suicide Squad" and wants to prove herself

00:02:22.882 --> 00:02:24.242
all over again.

00:02:24.242 --> 00:02:27.972
As Waller herself later says, "Barbie's ambitious
– watch out for her."

00:02:28.972 --> 00:02:33.892
Somewhat surprisingly, Viola Davis has a short
cameo in the first episode as Amanda Waller.

00:02:33.892 --> 00:02:38.452
She appears in a short video call with Leota,
who, in addition to working as Waller's eyes

00:02:38.452 --> 00:02:41.542
and ears on this mission, also happens to
be her daughter.

00:02:41.542 --> 00:02:46.062
In keeping with her usual M.O., Waller is
once again playing a game outside the bounds

00:02:46.062 --> 00:02:47.672
of the stated mission.

00:02:47.672 --> 00:02:52.482
During her FaceTime call with Leota, Waller
commands her to hide a forged diary in Peacemaker's

00:02:52.482 --> 00:02:55.902
trailer, for reasons that are initially known
only to her.

00:02:55.902 --> 00:03:00.012
The exact purpose of the diary may not be
made immediately clear, but given the crying

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:04.552
child on the cover, it's likely to paint a
less-than-flattering picture of Peacemaker's

00:03:04.552 --> 00:03:05.992
inner psyche.

00:03:05.992 --> 00:03:07.122
But to what end?

00:03:07.122 --> 00:03:11.012
While Amanda Waller's exact plan in the "Peacemaker"
series remains unclear in the first three

00:03:11.012 --> 00:03:15.642
episodes, it seems certain that Waller will
seek to double cross Peacemaker and the rest

00:03:15.642 --> 00:03:16.642
of the team eventually.

00:03:17.642 --> 00:03:21.512
Leota's not the only character in "Peacemaker"
with an interesting parent who is difficult

00:03:21.512 --> 00:03:22.512
to deal with.

00:03:22.512 --> 00:03:27.762
"Terminator 2" star Robert Patrick plays Peacemaker's
appallingly racist father, Auggie.

00:03:27.762 --> 00:03:31.952
When Peacemaker first arrives at his dad's
home, his dad is visibly displeased to see

00:03:31.952 --> 00:03:32.952
him.

00:03:32.952 --> 00:03:36.452
While Auggie is briefly amused at the story
of Bloodsport's childhood trauma, his main

00:03:36.452 --> 00:03:40.152
response to his son's war stories is rooted
in disappointment.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:43.962
At his son's insistence, Auggie gives him
another Peacemaker-branded helmet.

00:03:43.962 --> 00:03:48.952
As it turns out, Peacemaker's new helmet ends
up coming his way at just the right time.

00:03:48.952 --> 00:03:53.842
After getting rejected by Harcourt, Peacemaker
goes home with Annie, a random woman at the

00:03:53.842 --> 00:03:54.842
bar.

00:03:54.842 --> 00:03:58.072
Unfortunately, as their casual encounter is
on the cusp of wrapping up, that same woman

00:03:58.072 --> 00:04:02.872
seems to go completely feral, stabbing Peacemaker
and throwing him through a wall.

00:04:02.872 --> 00:04:06.712
It isn't until Peacemaker is reunited with
his helmet that he is able to gain the upper

00:04:06.712 --> 00:04:10.542
hand by activating a new feature: the sonic
boom.

00:04:10.542 --> 00:04:14.092
Considering how effective Augie's helmet tech
seems to be in this first episode, we can't

00:04:14.092 --> 00:04:18.191
help but wonder if these other helmets will
be utilized at some other point this season.

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:22.922
The other power-up options in the lab offer
features as varied as a full body force field,

00:04:22.922 --> 00:04:26.442
an underwater breathing apparatus, and X-ray
vision tech.

00:04:26.442 --> 00:04:31.482
In a post-credits sequence, Auggie even shows
Peacemaker a helmet that literally just infects

00:04:31.482 --> 00:04:34.262
its wearer with scabies– just because.

00:04:34.262 --> 00:04:38.992
"Why would I want scabies?"

00:04:38.992 --> 00:04:41.932
"To challenge yourself.

00:04:41.932 --> 00:04:44.232
Every man should have scabies once in his
life."

00:04:45.246 --> 00:04:49.602
The motivations for Annie Sturphausen's attack
on Peacemaker in the first episode aren't

00:04:49.602 --> 00:04:51.792
entirely clear to the team at first.

00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:56.001
Murn notes that the entire operation has been
kept off the books and he can't understand

00:04:56.001 --> 00:04:58.792
how anyone could have known that Peacemaker
was a part of it.

00:04:58.792 --> 00:05:02.031
Harcourt suggests that Amanda Waller might
have been behind it.

00:05:02.031 --> 00:05:06.632
After Leota insists that it's not Waller,
Harcourt even begins to question Leota's placement

00:05:06.632 --> 00:05:07.632
on the mission.

00:05:07.632 --> 00:05:11.422
Eventually, however, Peacemaker remembers
that he caught Annie reviewing the classified

00:05:11.422 --> 00:05:16.471
materials provided to him by Murn, including
a dossier detailing the mission to assassinate

00:05:16.471 --> 00:05:18.292
a sitting U.S. Senator.

00:05:18.292 --> 00:05:23.192
While Harcourt is proven wrong in her initial
accusations against Leota, this specific encounter

00:05:23.192 --> 00:05:26.402
has clearly raised her suspicions of her newest
colleague.

00:05:26.402 --> 00:05:30.442
We can't imagine that Harcourt or any of the
other team members will react positively when

00:05:30.442 --> 00:05:34.762
they find out that Waller and Leota are keeping
an important part of the mission plan a secret.

00:05:35.762 --> 00:05:39.591
We can't call it entirely shocking to discover
that Peacemaker's father is a character like

00:05:39.591 --> 00:05:40.591
White Dragon.

00:05:40.591 --> 00:05:45.012
Auggie Smith isn't exactly excited to see
his son return home and he's quickly revealed

00:05:45.012 --> 00:05:47.091
to be a vile homophobe and racist.

00:05:47.091 --> 00:05:52.151
Now that Auggie finds himself in prison after
John Economos frames him for Peacemaker's

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:56.621
crimes, he is shown to command a vast number
of fiercely loyal white supremacist followers.

00:05:56.621 --> 00:06:00.801
In some ways, this is a fitting adaptation
from the "Peacemaker" comic book series, in

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:05.732
which, Peacemaker's father, Wolfgang Schmidt,
is a former commandant of a Nazi concentration

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:07.672
camp during World War II.

00:06:07.672 --> 00:06:12.912
Since the last concentration camp was liberated
by the Allies in May of 1945 and "Peacemaker"

00:06:12.912 --> 00:06:17.061
is set in the present day, the math wouldn't
quite allow for the same origin story without

00:06:17.061 --> 00:06:18.202
some changes.

00:06:18.202 --> 00:06:23.281
In the comics, William Heller (aka White Dragon)
is unrelated to Peacemaker, but considering

00:06:23.281 --> 00:06:28.112
the comic character's white supremicist motivations
and appearances in the "Suicide Squad" comic

00:06:28.112 --> 00:06:31.751
books, this new configuration turns out to
be a natural fit.

00:06:32.871 --> 00:06:36.361
Peacemaker is definitely one of those characters
who just seems to stumble into Earth-shattering

00:06:36.361 --> 00:06:37.581
revelations.

00:06:37.581 --> 00:06:42.192
After a long set of failures, Vigilante convinces
Peacemaker to let loose by celebrating his

00:06:42.192 --> 00:06:46.961
release from prison with a mixture of controlled
substances, firearms, and explosives.

00:06:46.961 --> 00:06:51.471
However, the day's festivities don't stop
Peacemaker from mistakenly learning more about

00:06:51.471 --> 00:06:52.852
his upcoming mission.

00:06:52.852 --> 00:06:57.111
While smoking marijuana with Vigilante and
Amber, Peacemaker starts fiddling around with

00:06:57.111 --> 00:06:59.801
the alien-looking device he stole from Annie's
house.

00:06:59.801 --> 00:07:03.852
When Peacemaker touches a button on the device,
it quickly expands and forms what appears

00:07:03.852 --> 00:07:05.692
to be a tiny spaceship.

00:07:05.692 --> 00:07:10.262
By the time the second episode wraps up, it's
unclear who or what purpose such a small vessel

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:14.121
could serve – but it has to be tied to Project
Butterfly somehow.

00:07:15.232 --> 00:07:19.531
Episode 3 puts the deadly capabilities of
Vigilante on display for the first time.

00:07:19.531 --> 00:07:23.651
Following Peacemaker's inability to pull the
trigger at the home of Senator Royland Goff,

00:07:23.651 --> 00:07:27.531
Vigilante takes control of the mission by
executing three of the four targets.

00:07:27.531 --> 00:07:32.751
After Peacemaker and Vigilante are captured
by Goff, Vigilante is unmasked and tortured.

00:07:32.751 --> 00:07:37.422
Unfortunately for Vigilante, Peacemaker refuses
to give up any information, even going so

00:07:37.422 --> 00:07:40.952
far as to tell Goff to basically do his worst,
torture-wise.

00:07:40.952 --> 00:07:42.602
"Does that change your mind?"

00:07:42.602 --> 00:07:44.811
"Sorry pal – not for sale."

00:07:44.811 --> 00:07:45.811
"What?"

00:07:45.811 --> 00:07:47.341
"Give it all you got!"

00:07:47.341 --> 00:07:51.612
Vigilante is visibly shocked when Peacemaker
refuses to spare him any torture and appears

00:07:51.612 --> 00:07:54.942
genuinely hurt at Peacemaker's lack of empathy
for him.

00:07:54.942 --> 00:07:59.192
Given Peacemaker's prior actions, what could
possibly make Vigilante surprised by Peacemaker's

00:07:59.192 --> 00:08:00.892
unflinching response?

00:08:00.892 --> 00:08:03.961
Maybe Vigilante really is as delusional as
he's seemed to be.

00:08:03.961 --> 00:08:09.181
Still, even if Vigilante is Peacemaker's number
one fan, losing part of a pinky toe is bound

00:08:09.181 --> 00:08:11.861
to drive a wedge into even the hardiest of
friendships.

00:08:11.861 --> 00:08:16.281
It doesn't seem like these two would-be superheroes
are quite that close to begin with.

00:08:16.281 --> 00:08:17.602
"Dude, I'm your best friend."

00:08:17.602 --> 00:08:18.602
"No, you're not."

00:08:19.602 --> 00:08:23.471
To quote Ned Leeds of "Spider-Man: Homecoming",
most people would probably agree that John

00:08:23.471 --> 00:08:26.531
Economos seems like an archetypical "guy in
the chair."

00:08:26.531 --> 00:08:28.341
"Can I be your guy in the chair?"

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:29.341
"What?"

00:08:29.341 --> 00:08:36.062
"You know how there's a guy with a headset
telling the other guy where to go?"

00:08:36.062 --> 00:08:40.362
However, Episode 3 forces Economos to quite
literally jump out of his chair and face a

00:08:40.362 --> 00:08:41.772
threat directly.

00:08:41.772 --> 00:08:46.162
As Harcourt, Leota, and Murn move in on the
house where Peacemaker and Vigilante are held

00:08:46.162 --> 00:08:51.402
hostage by a Butterfly, Economos realizes
that Judo Master is escaping the scene in

00:08:51.402 --> 00:08:52.402
a vehicle.

00:08:52.402 --> 00:08:56.732
John ultimately rises to the occasion, crashing
the team's van directly into Judomaster's

00:08:56.732 --> 00:09:00.002
car and later pummeling the martial artist
with a tire iron.

00:09:00.002 --> 00:09:04.102
That might be a big win for John's ego, but
the bigger question is where Judo Master was

00:09:04.102 --> 00:09:05.102
driving to.

00:09:05.102 --> 00:09:08.712
Before Goff starts to torture Vigilante for
answers, he tells Judo Master,

00:09:08.712 --> 00:09:11.612
"Take the tunnel to the forest.

00:09:11.612 --> 00:09:15.932
From there, get to Glen Tyler and let them
know what's occurred here."

00:09:15.932 --> 00:09:17.492
"Yes."

00:09:17.492 --> 00:09:21.832
Presumably these are other Butterflies, maybe
even more important ones than the senator.

00:09:21.832 --> 00:09:25.342
Once they find out about Peacemaker's mission,
how are they going to react?

00:09:25.849 --> 00:09:30.492
After Peacemaker gains the upper-hand against
Senator Goff, he fires a single shotgun blast

00:09:30.492 --> 00:09:31.982
into Goff's face.

00:09:31.982 --> 00:09:33.432
And that's that, right?

00:09:33.432 --> 00:09:37.702
In most cases, this would mean the end of
Goff's character, but not on "Peacemaker."

00:09:37.702 --> 00:09:41.552
As Peacemaker and Vigilante prepare to reunite
with the rest of the team upstairs, the two

00:09:41.552 --> 00:09:44.742
notice a small creature crawling out of the
face of the late senator.

00:09:44.742 --> 00:09:50.872
As the creature takes to the sky with a flapping
of its wings, Peacemaker knowingly remarks,

00:09:50.872 --> 00:09:56.182
"Oh, Project Butterfly."

00:09:56.182 --> 00:09:59.662
That's when the episode ends with a tease
that "suspected butterflies" are all over

00:09:59.662 --> 00:10:00.902
the world.

00:10:00.902 --> 00:10:04.922
Episode 3's reveal of the literal butterfly
inside Senator Goff's head is a major clue

00:10:04.922 --> 00:10:09.982
to the entire mission at large, a subject
about which Peacemaker actually knows frighteningly

00:10:09.982 --> 00:10:10.982
little.

00:10:10.982 --> 00:10:14.902
Is the goal to kill all butterflies, or just
the ones that Amanda Waller wants dead?

00:10:14.902 --> 00:10:18.592
When Peacemaker gives Murn intel that proves
that the seemingly happy family of four is

00:10:18.592 --> 00:10:22.982
actually entirely composed of Butterflies,
the task force captain quickly relays orders

00:10:22.982 --> 00:10:23.982
to kill them all.

00:10:23.982 --> 00:10:28.242
Does this mean all Butterflies are as dangerous
as the woman who attacks Peacemaker in Episode

00:10:28.242 --> 00:10:29.242
1?

00:10:29.242 --> 00:10:32.372
Considering the fact that we've only seen
them attack Peacemaker either in self-defense

00:10:32.372 --> 00:10:36.402
or after discovering his assassination plan,
they might not even be malevolent.

00:10:36.402 --> 00:10:40.602
Regardless, given everything we've learned
about the group so far, it seems fairly obvious

00:10:40.602 --> 00:10:45.032
that literally anyone, even people we think
we know, could secretly be a butterfly.

00:10:46.032 --> 00:10:50.352
Many of the post-credits scenes in "Peacemaker"
work as jokey extensions of scenes from the

00:10:50.352 --> 00:10:53.702
episode, rather than material that's critical
to the plot.

00:10:53.702 --> 00:10:57.342
Episode 3's post-credits sequence takes us
back to the moment when Vigilante reveals

00:10:57.342 --> 00:11:00.722
himself behind the bushes outside the home
of Senator Goff.

00:11:00.722 --> 00:11:05.143
As Harcourt prepares for the possibility that
Vigilante could ruin the entire mission, she

00:11:05.143 --> 00:11:06.432
issues a menacing threat.

00:11:06.432 --> 00:11:10.262
"If you f— up this mission, I will kill
your f—in' family."

00:11:10.262 --> 00:11:11.262
"Ok.

00:11:11.262 --> 00:11:12.262
Good luck!

00:11:12.262 --> 00:11:13.902
A little late for that...

00:11:13.902 --> 00:11:16.602
You guys got beer?"

00:11:16.602 --> 00:11:20.602
Considering this character's particular proclivity
for violence, it doesn't seem like a big stretch

00:11:20.602 --> 00:11:25.162
to guess that Vigilante might even be the
one responsible for his family's deaths.

00:11:25.162 --> 00:11:29.562
In the "Vigilante" comic series, Adrian Chase
takes on the Vigilante persona after his wife

00:11:29.562 --> 00:11:31.362
and children are murdered by the mob.

00:11:31.362 --> 00:11:35.222
While it's possible this series is simply
alluding to the original character's comic

00:11:35.222 --> 00:11:39.842
history, we think it's more likely this character
has an intensely more absurd background.

00:11:39.842 --> 00:11:43.932
In Episode 2, Vigilante admits to Peacemaker
that, in prior years, he would have killed

00:11:43.932 --> 00:11:48.462
him for smoking marijuana, and he seems similarly
extreme in his response to other crimes.

00:11:48.462 --> 00:11:55.412
"When I found out someone murdered an innocent
person or sold someone heroin or did some

00:11:55.412 --> 00:11:58.322
grafitti and I kill that person…"

00:11:58.322 --> 00:12:02.902
Perhaps Vigilante's family members simply
chose a bad time to jaywalk?

